# Event-driven external waits

When CI or Jira work requires waiting, do not poll, use `--watch`, retry with
sleep, or keep reasoning until a status changes. Use the deployed receiver:

- Register the pending wait with `POST https://agent-waiter.vercel.app/api/tasks`.
- The request must use the host's configured bearer credential; never expose or
  request a secret in chat, code, logs, or commits.
- Include a unique `taskHandle`, the original OpenAI `callId`, an HTTPS
  `resumeUrl`, the provider resource ID, and an expiration time.
- For GitHub, include `githubEvent` as `workflow_run` or `check_run`.
- For Jira, include the Jira resource ID and explicit
  `jiraTerminalStatusIds`. A Jira webhook only resumes a registered task when
  its status changes to one of those IDs.

After registration, end the model turn and let the signed callback resume the
host. The production webhooks are already configured at:

- `https://agent-waiter.vercel.app/api/github`
- `https://agent-waiter.vercel.app/api/jira`

A single read-only diagnostic lookup is allowed to choose the next action. If
the active agent host cannot register a task or receive an HTTPS callback,
report that integration gap instead of polling.
